@startuml SSD-S1-receive-delivery
' System sequence diagram for UC-02 Receive delivery (+ UC-11), slice S1
' Black-box view: one actor, the system as a single lifeline, system events and returned outcomes only
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

title SSD-S1 Receive delivery (UC-02, UC-11)

actor "Hub volunteer\n(or staff / manager)" as V
participant ":KerryHubSystem" as S

alt expected delivery exists
  V -> S : startReceipt(producerId, deliveryId)
  S --> V : ReceiptView (deliveryId, expected lines)
else unannounced delivery (1a)
  V -> S : startReceipt(producerId, none)
  S --> V : ReceiptView (deliveryId, unannounced, no lines)
  loop for each product delivered
    V -> S : addLine(deliveryId, productId)
    S --> V : deliveryLineId
  end
end

loop for each line that arrived
  V -> S : recordLineReceipt(deliveryLineId, supplied: Quantity,\n  trace: TraceDetails, outcome: ReceiptOutcome,\n  accepted: Quantity, reason)
  alt valid and permitted
    S --> V : LineReceiptResult (received, available, held, lotId?)
  else actor not permitted to reject (6c)
    S --> V : Failure(NOT_PERMITTED)
  else accepted > received, accepted = 0, or no unit conversion (4a, 6e)
    S --> V : Failure(INVALID_QUANTITY)
  else use-by before delivery date (UC-11 3a)
    S --> V : Failure(INVALID_TRACE)
  end
end

V -> S : completeReceipt(deliveryId)
S --> V : ReceiptSummary (available and held per product,\n differences from expected, lines not received,\n lines needing batch follow-up)

note over V, S
  Abandoning (9a) is not a system event: the volunteer simply stops.
  Recorded lines keep their outcomes; the receipt stays open (RC-07).
end note
@enduml